/-
# TokenCensus.Table — the census of private constructors

The table `TokenCensus` checks (see `TokenCensus/Core.lean` for the checks). It is a
Lean module, not a loose text file, so that Lake rebuilds the census whenever a row
changes. One row per private constructor of a package type:

    constructor | home module | layer | reason
-/

namespace Minidregg.TokenCensus

/-- The census table, one row per line; `#` starts a comment line. -/
def table : String := "
# Token census: every private constructor of a package type (TokenCensus.lean checks this table).
# Columns:  constructor | home module | layer | reason
#   layer  L1 <theorem>         the type carries the proposition it asserts: <theorem> ranges over every
#                               inhabitant, says something about it and names its indices (checked)
#          restricted <fn,fn>   a provenance token with no proposition: only the named functions mint
#                               it, and each has a `restrict` row pinning its callers (check 6)
#          defect <cv task>     reviewed and found NOT to carry its guarantee; the task fixes it; the
#                               merge gate refuses a commit that adds a defect row
# There is no unreviewed layer. A type whose privacy guards nothing is not a token: it is not private.
# The reason says in words what the witness states about which indices (rows reviewed 2026-10-14,
# lane census-review, by reading each statement).
Minidregg.Assurance.ReactiveLifecycleHistory.Broken.mk | Assurance.ReactiveLifecycleHistory | L1 Minidregg.Assurance.ReactiveLifecycleHistory.Broken.authorizedBreak | rules.Breaks spec.cancelRequest reason entry.context entry.claim: the retained authenticated history entry is recognized by the Lean rules as a break under the promise's exact eager cancellation request
Minidregg.Assurance.ReactiveLifecycleHistory.Expired.mk | Assurance.ReactiveLifecycleHistory | L1 Minidregg.Assurance.ReactiveLifecycleHistory.Expired.afterDeadline | spec.deadline < rules.observedHeight entry.context: the canonically projected height of the retained authenticated entry is strictly after the promise's deadline
